# Fights at Reorte, a dictatorship 4.4 light years from Lave, and meets the Boa, Cobra Mk I, Gecko and
# Fer-de-Lance, which no other replay meets. It starts from combat-reorte.cdr (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py): the
# fighter (a military laser, ECM, an energy unit, 20 kills) with its random state 4,148,768 draws on. It finds
# Reorte on the short-range chart and jumps there. In space it holds J and full speed whenever no ship but a rock
# or a barrel is about: while the jump drive is engaged, ships of every class spawn 32 times as often
# (ScaleSpawnOdds) until a ship mass-locks the drive. The draw count was found by a search over counts for the run
# that meets the most ship types the rest of the corpus does not. The fight was played by a scratch program that
# steered at the nearest ship by its position each frame and fired when it was in the sights; what it pressed is
# recorded here like any other replay.
file JAMESON.CDR combat-reorte.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # the disc menu
key l; wait 0.3                    # Load Commander: it asks for a file name
key j; key a; key m; key e; key s; key o; key n; key Return; wait 0.5
digest loaded 1a9546b2667ef2cd9ad93c8743688459259a13a05a46d41fa43253a779644dfd
key F6; wait 0.5                   # the short-range chart: F finds a system by name
key f; wait 0.3; key r; key e; key o; key r; key t; key e; key Return; wait 0.3
key F1; wait 0.5                   # launch
down h; wait 1; up h               # the countdown to Reorte
wait 8
digest reorte 1374aa211aae78e344736c00482664515ebb82489401ba8d0326411049515081
# The fight, as recorded: a step for each change of the keys, and the frames between.
